{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "No evidence-supported optimization cleanly applies to this workflow without violating a contraindication or lacking a precondition. P-LIT-GHA-CACHE (dependency caching) has no dependency-installation step to cache. P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT already has timeout-minutes: 10 and there is insufficient representative history to justify tightening without false-timeout risk. P-LIT-IDLE-SCHEDULE is contraindicated because results depend on external GitHub star activity and time-based freshness, not only repository changes. P-LIT-FAIL-SCHEDULE requires an approved pause/resume policy that is not established, and periodic star-history checks may be mandatory. P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE is contraindicated because the workflow performs commit and pull-request publishing work; canceling a superseded run mid-publish could leave branches/PRs in an inconsistent state. The synthetic experiment records (P-LIT-DURATION-PREDICTION, P-LIT-UNUSED-DEP-SKIP, P-LIT-IDLE-SCHEDULE) explicitly state they are scenario resource costs, not real repository CI savings, and establish no real cron pause, build omission, or prediction accuracy. The workflow is already tightly scoped, allowlisted, and timeout-bounded, so changing it risks weakening its safety controls.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT", "P-LIT-IDLE-SCHEDULE", "P-LIT-FAIL-SCHEDULE", "P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE"]
}
